{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals","id":1173250,"title":"C20 - Kinain Prodigals...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-04T09:53:22-08:00","id":1173250,"title":"C20 - Kinain Prodigals...","content":"Having finally been able to read over the C20 book I was thrilled at how Kinain are done. However, someone immediately brought up that Fae Blood is a 4 point merit for Mages and Werewolves. Considering all that Kinain get (Glamour, a Birthright, 1 art and 2 realms) this seems way too powerful for such a merit.<br /> <br /> Is there some drawback I am missing, or should someone taking that merit use the old Enchanted rules where everything needs to be paid for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8764-zulkir-jhor","name":"Zulkir Jhor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T13:58:41-08:00","id":1173317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zulkir Jhor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals#post1173250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having finally been able to read over the C20 book I was thrilled at how Kinain are done. However, someone immediately brought up that Fae Blood is a 4 point merit for Mages and Werewolves. Considering all that Kinain get (Glamour, a Birthright, 1 art and 2 realms) this seems way too powerful for such a merit.<br /> <br /> Is there some drawback I am missing, or should someone taking that merit use the old Enchanted rules where everything needs to be paid for?</div> </div> </div> </div>For a point of comparison, the likes of Silver Tolerance and Immune to Wyrm Emanations aren't much more expensive (6-7 vs 4). Merits have never really been the height of sensible balance. Or even a small amount of it, for that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T15:11:54-08:00","id":1173338,"title":"","content":"I think going with having to pay for the Glamour, Arts and Realms separately should generally be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T20:12:33-08:00","id":1173402,"title":"","content":"To be fair I doubt the people who wrote it had kinain and their powers in mind. Personally I'd just house rule the merits out of existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T20:50:43-08:00","id":1173405,"title":"","content":"kinain rules are not built for crossover. They are built for playing KInain in a changeling game. We see prodigals written up similarly in the book with Arts and Realms. IF running a Prodigal using its &quot;proper game&quot; with Fae blood my suggestion is to not give them the additional Arts or the Faeblood background as they already have theirown innate powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T22:57:12-08:00","id":1173418,"title":"","content":"Hail!<br /> <br /> In WoD, (as I understand it) the old rules overwrites the old ones, but if something hasn't been touched, the old ones stands.<br /> <br /> In multiple older rulebooks it's stated that powers of different beeings don't mesh well.<br /> <br /> Werewolf / Kinfolk with Gnosis can't have Glamour, Mages can't use Arts, etc.<br /> <br /> What you would possible get for your merit are:<br /> Standing with Kinain;<br /> Lower Banality;<br /> A new, but mainly useless Background (Fae Blood);<br /> Birthright (awesome).<br /> <br /> Personaly I loved the Revised rules better. I don't really know why did they grinded down the rules and gave us these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T00:12:58-08:00","id":1173428,"title":"","content":"Birthrights are abit better costed than Legendary attribute if you give it with Fae blood, but its really one point plus legendary attribute gives you a special trick with it so.<br /> <br /> One other thing I'd do if I had a fae blooded Shifter is put all the &quot;Fae&quot; type gifts treated as in tribe for them even if they aren't generally available to them at all(like Ceilican and Fianna gifts that they don't share)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T00:30:07-08:00","id":1173431,"title":"","content":"I'd generally say Fae Blooded Prodigals don't get the Glamour/Art/Realm bonuses if you are using the different gamelines' full mechanics together. At most I'd suggest allowing them access to faerie-tie in powers thematic to their kind even if they wouldn't otherwise qualify for them (i.e. Fae-Blooded Vampires can learn Mythercia without needing to feed on the blood of a Kiasyd teacher. Fae-Blooded Werewolves can learn the appropriate Fianna Gifts via their Changeling relatives even if they aren't Fianna; Fae-Blooded Mages can just incorporate faerie lore and the Dreaming into their paradigm, and may have justification to treat faerie-folklore-themed effects as less Vulgar than they'd be for other Mages, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T01:31:56-08:00","id":1173439,"title":"","content":"I am of the opinion that mixing powers/power stats between splats is a bad idea. So my suggestion is don\u2019t do it.<br /> <br /> As for how to handle Fae blooded Merit within the other splats...<br /> <br /> For Vampires this is simple as V20, and V20: DA, have given us better rules for feablooded Vampires. So for them I suggest using the Maeghar \u201dbloodline\u201d and rules associated with it (from The Black Hand: A Guide to the TalkMahe\u2019Ra) or the rules for Kiasyd (the rules found in V20: DA that is) depending on circumstaces and books available to you. Kiasyd, as in Marconius brood, who can reliably embrace more of their kind, including shared appearance trait and discipline set, are just obviously results of experimentation with the Sevartal.<br /> <br /> For Mages I\u2019d just use the Merit as described in M20 Book of Secrets, that is permanent enchantment and low Banality. I\u2019d also allow one to use it as a reason to buy other supernatural merits, like Legendary Attribute Etc. I also might allow some effects to be cast coincidentally if they would be rotes relying on your Fae heritage.<br /> <br /> For the Garou I\u2019m not sure if there is a Fae Blood merit for W20 anywhere but probably would just take a page from Mage and go with low Banality and permanent enchantment. Though I would likely also give access to Fae related gifts as well.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately we dont yet have Wraith20 but in general aside from possibly odd appearance for their corpus, and possibly some memories of such existence, they would have affinity with the Phantasm and Pandemonium arcanoi or possibly just use the Keremet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T02:45:49-08:00","id":1173457,"title":"","content":"Honestly Low banality, permanent enchantment and a birthright isn't a broken level of merits especially since low banality means you are weaker to fae magic, as does permanent enchantment. Most of the Birthrights are less powerful than Legendary attribute(and I wouldn't let someone stack them) there are some that are abit more powerful but they suggest not saying handing out a pooka's shapeshift to Kinain anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-07T06:38:41-08:00","id":1174007,"title":"","content":"Run with it as it's written in the book it comes from with tweaks to make it not silly in crossovers. Kinain can have children who are changelings. I'm not sure where the &quot;faerie blood&quot; merit comes from but it's not in the 20th anniversary merits in the core books and I doubt it's intention is to let the character have changeling children. So I think you're fine with saying a character with that merit is not a kinain at all but still loosely blood related to them. Distant cousins rather than a part of the direct family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23656-lanir","name":"Lanir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T02:21:20-08:00","id":1176224,"title":"","content":"IIRC, mages can't ever have a Glamour rating, and this probably applies to other supernaturals too. I think I read this in one of the old FAQs back in the day.<br /> <br /> Officially, it's to do with your Avatar (or the equivalent part of your soul): mages' Avatars are Awakened to their own power; fae Avatars are bound to the Dreaming; Garou Avatars are bound to Gaia; Kindred Avatars are bound to the blood; mummy Avatars are bound to Ma'at, etc. So that essentially means you can only have one mystical tie to the universe at any given time. Mages have Arete and Quintessence, so they can't have Glamour too.<br /> <br /> If a mage were to carry faerie blood, it wouldn't manifest as it does in pure Kinain. As others have said, they might be able to mimic Arts and Realms through their Spheres (possibly conferring the benefits of coincidental magic), but they don't have those traits, per se. Certain Kinain Backgrounds may be fair game, and I may give the character a Birthright, but they couldn't buy the Fae Blood Background or do anything that would require a Glamour roll (although I'd allow them to substitute Quintessence for Glamour where they need to spend points).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T20:56:21-08:00","id":1176454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1176224#post1176224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, mages can't ever have a Glamour rating, and this probably applies to other supernaturals too. I think I read this in one of the old FAQs back in the day.<br /> <br /> Officially, it's to do with your Avatar (or the equivalent part of your soul): mages' Avatars are Awakened to their own power; fae Avatars are bound to the Dreaming; Garou Avatars are bound to Gaia; Kindred Avatars are bound to the blood; mummy Avatars are bound to Ma'at, etc. So that essentially means you can only have one mystical tie to the universe at any given time. Mages have Arete and Quintessence, so they can't have Glamour too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The avatar explanation is only for Mage. Everything else just notes that Glamour is a competing power (as in Werewolf, and probably others), or not something that they can use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a mage were to carry faerie blood, it wouldn't manifest as it does in pure Kinain. As others have said, they might be able to mimic Arts and Realms through their Spheres (possibly conferring the benefits of coincidental magic), but they don't have those traits, per se. Certain Kinain Backgrounds may be fair game, and I may give the character a Birthright, but they couldn't buy the Fae Blood Background or do anything that would require a Glamour roll (although I'd allow them to substitute Quintessence for Glamour where they need to spend points). </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't let trying to fake Arts and Realms be coincidental. That's like trying to fake Gifts - you're not Garou or Fera, so you shouldn't be able to do it unless it's one of the very low-powered ones that kin could conceivably learn, and it'd lock you into a fixed pattern of what rotes you can use based on what kin could likely know and use altogether, so a vast array of effects while trying to play in these rules would be out of the question. With Arts and Realms, I'd expect something even more stringent, with the possibility of using the Dreaming getting angry at you as a potential stand-in for Paradox. Don't try to cheat two systems at once. It doesn't tend to work out too well, especially if you have to live in one and want to be friendly to the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T19:26:06-08:00","id":1176668,"title":"","content":"What I find amusing is that everyone ignores the most important part of those Merits. The fae are willing to talk to you. In the case of the Garou, they don't kill you on sight. Those can be pretty big benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23716-scottish","name":"Scottish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T19:42:13-08:00","id":1176671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scottish</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1176668#post1176668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I find amusing is that everyone ignores the most important part of those Merits. The fae are willing to talk to you. In the case of the Garou, they don't kill you on sight. Those can be pretty big benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings are willing to talk to whoever. There is a rule about not talking to mortals, but the question of if that applies to Prodigals is probably even more of a question of talking to Kinain anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, the real big advantage of being Kinain, being enchanted and thus being able to see and remember the fae, is lost if you can't also manipulate Glamour, and most people here are suggesting that Prodigals can't do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T20:04:34-08:00","id":1176677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1176671#post1176671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changelings are willing to talk to whoever. There is a rule about not talking to mortals, but the question of if that applies to Prodigals is probably even more of a question of talking to Kinain anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, the real big advantage of being Kinain, being enchanted and thus being able to see and remember the fae, is lost if you can't also manipulate Glamour, and most people here are suggesting that Prodigals can't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the reputation of mages as Glamour-thieves, being willing to talk is a pretty big benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23716-scottish","name":"Scottish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T20:46:32-08:00","id":1177152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1176671#post1176671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changelings are willing to talk to whoever. There is a rule about not talking to mortals, but the question of if that applies to Prodigals is probably even more of a question of talking to Kinain anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, the real big advantage of being Kinain, being enchanted and thus being able to see and remember the fae, is lost if you can't also manipulate Glamour, and most people here are suggesting that Prodigals can't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its not that perse I just prefer the Kiasyd solution vs going Sam Haight on it. Use your &quot;main&quot; Splat with some of the other game's flavor as a Kinain vs &quot;I Get Gifts, and spheres, and arts...&quot; They don't get a separate glamour pool though they may spend Quint or Gnosis or Maybe even Rage for general things. They get their birthright. They get to incorporate Faerie themes into their base setup(Gifts with Faerie descriptors PERHAPS some based one Arts but they still are GIFTS.) they don't get two separate pools of magic unless they already have multiple supernatural pools ala Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T04:46:57-08:00","id":1177236,"title":"","content":"And I'm saying that framework doesn't work with Changeling. Maybe a Mage could create a Glamour pool, and maybe Dross could be used as well, but having say a Werewolf kinain not be able to use Glamour means from a Changeling perspective that they're not kinain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T05:12:30-08:00","id":1177239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177236#post1177236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm saying that framework doesn't work with Changeling. Maybe a Mage could create a Glamour pool, and maybe Dross could be used as well, but having say a Werewolf kinain not be able to use Glamour means from a Changeling perspective that they're not kinain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why so?<br /> <br /> And to answer my own question you are of course correct in the sense of them being actually being werewolves, or to be accurate Garou, with Fae blood not full blown kinain. But I\u2019d say permanent enchantment and ability to remember the Fae make them quite kinain enough to count as such from both Kithain and Garou perspectives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T06:29:29-08:00","id":1177255,"title":"","content":"I guess I see the Glamour Regeneration mechanic of a kinain is intimetely tied to being permanently enchanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T06:39:40-08:00","id":1177257,"title":"","content":"Re-reading that chapter in C20, I can't see anything about the Faerie Blood Merit. I think it's specific to other gamelines. Ergo, having the Merit doesn't make you kinain, it just makes you a blood relative of a faerie. Not all faeries' relatives get the benefits of being kinain. You only get the watered down benefits listed in the relevant core book for the being you're playing.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a full-blooded kinain, as it were, you'd start with the C20 rules but wouldn't be able to Awaken or become a werewolf. You probably can't become Imbued, either, as your connection to the Dreaming would taint you. You could become a vampire, but you'd lose your kinain powers, although you may become Maeghar if your ST is *very* generous. You potentially could become a Sorcerer, though, and you could become a ghoul.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's enough to buy the Faerie Blood Merit and then apply the kinain template on top.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T07:38:55-08:00","id":1177277,"title":"","content":"It is for other game lines, so you can play a kinain that Awakened/Changed. Your Banality is lower, and you are permanently enchanted. It can't be taken if you're a technomancer. Which only makes sense if the designers ever saw a Son of Ether vs. nocker mad science contest. If any technomaner could be nocker/Dougal kinain, it's the Etherites. But, they can tend to end up dominating a game with those contests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23716-scottish","name":"Scottish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T07:59:11-08:00","id":1177284,"title":"","content":"Restricting based on Tradition/Convention is pretty silly. Although in most scenarios having a kinain NWO/syndicate/etc would be very, very bad for the local Changeling population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T08:23:04-08:00","id":1177300,"title":"","content":"It's paradigm, not Tradition/Convention. You can be a technomancer in any Tradition/Craft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23716-scottish","name":"Scottish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T08:33:37-08:00","id":1177303,"title":"","content":"That makes no sense though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T09:28:32-08:00","id":1177328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177236#post1177236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm saying that framework doesn't work with Changeling. Maybe a Mage could create a Glamour pool, and maybe Dross could be used as well, but having say a Werewolf kinain not be able to use Glamour means from a Changeling perspective that they're not kinain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think you are getting what i am saying at all.<br /> <br /> In my theoretical setup a Mage does have a Glamour pool, its called Quintessence. They have a Single Pool of &quot;MAGIC SHIT&quot; that can be used for general changeling stuff(like oaths, can be stolen through Ravaging etc) and general mage stuff(decreasing difficulty of effects, healing agg..) Dross functions as Tass for them.<br /> <br /> Similarly for a Kinain Fera, they have a pool that allows them to engage with Fairy stuff its called &quot;Gnosis&quot;. <br /> <br /> From a mage perspective they are all different flavours of Quint anyway. From a Changeling perspective its all Glamour too! Read over the writeups of protigals in c20 there's no &quot;hey they use completely different forms of magic to change the world&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T09:30:57-08:00","id":1177329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scottish</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177277#post1177277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is for other game lines, so you can play a kinain that Awakened/Changed. Your Banality is lower, and you are permanently enchanted. It can't be taken if you're a technomancer. Which only makes sense if the designers ever saw a Son of Ether vs. nocker mad science contest. If any technomaner could be nocker/Dougal kinain, it's the Etherites. But, they can tend to end up dominating a game with those contests.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, its because M20 is so slow they were working from 2e Changeling &quot;SCIENCE BADRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAWR&quot; and should probably be ignored when using c20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T09:34:43-08:00","id":1177332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177328#post1177328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think you are getting what i am saying at all.<br /> <br /> In my theoretical setup a Mage does have a Glamour pool, its called Quintessence. They have a Single Pool of &amp;quot;MAGIC SHIT&amp;quot; that can be used for general changeling stuff(like oaths, can be stolen through Ravaging etc) and general mage stuff(decreasing difficulty of effects, healing agg..) Dross functions as Tass for them.<br /> <br /> Similarly for a Kinain Fera, they have a pool that allows them to engage with Fairy stuff its called &amp;quot;Gnosis&amp;quot;. <br /> <br /> From a mage perspective they are all different flavours of Quint anyway. From a Changeling perspective its all Glamour too! Read over the writeups of protigals in c20 there's no &amp;quot;hey they use completely different forms of magic to change the world&amp;quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone will Glamour is enchanted. If you don't have Glamour you're not. Quint/Gnosis/Glamour/Blood/Rage/Pathos/Angst/Faith/Banality/Paradox are not all the same thing, although they all do contain a significant amount of Quint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T09:39:05-08:00","id":1177336,"title":"","content":"A tenchomancer is somebody who's entire way of working magic is scientific. They are not an end-user, and while you can supplement technology with mystic magic, a technomancer is all about making better technology. In another words, they're all about the science. The Technocracy is quite literally the defining standard of the technomancer. Everything goes in neat, orderly boxes that are clearly labeled. But, not every technomancer is like that. They live for the joy of finding or building something new, neat and cool. There's an entire Tradition full of those guys, but they aren't the only technomancers in the Traditions. Though the &quot;traditional&quot; technomancers of the Traditions are the Virtual Adepts, who could care less about the fae, and the Sons of Ether, who think they're all extinct. There are other technomancers in the Crafts and Traditions, but those are the big groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23716-scottish","name":"Scottish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T09:42:43-08:00","id":1177340,"title":"","content":"But it doesn't matter. Kinain don't have restrictions on Banality or whatnot, and technology and science aren't inherently Banal anyway. Heck, the Nockers certainly have a lot of Etherites in terms of outlook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T10:16:03-08:00","id":1177352,"title":"","content":"I'm not arguing that. Hell, it would make sense if half the Etherites were nocker-kin, and you can always house-rule it as you see fit. Honestly, I'd need to hear a pretty damned good story before okaying it. But that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23716-scottish","name":"Scottish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T10:29:37-08:00","id":1177357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177332#post1177332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone will Glamour is enchanted. If you don't have Glamour you're not. Quint/Gnosis/Glamour/Blood/Rage/Pathos/Angst/Faith/Banality/Paradox are not all the same thing, although they all do contain a significant amount of Quint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quint/Glamour/Gnosis are game mechanics to cover &quot;Magic shit pool&quot; if you'd prefer it gets renamed &quot;magic shit pool&quot; when someone is a kinain go right ahead.<br /> <br /> I see no reason for two pools. I see no reason to not allow them to use their generic magic pool multiple ways because they are Kinain. I see no reason to give mages or werewolves arts and realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T10:31:20-08:00","id":1177358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scottish</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177352#post1177352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not arguing that. Hell, it would make sense if half the Etherites were nocker-kin, and you can always house-rule it as you see fit. Honestly, I'd need to hear a pretty damned good story before okaying it. But that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's whole damned faction of Etherites called &quot;Adventurers&quot; so yeah someone who's hunted dinosaurs in the Hollow Earth is considered too banal to have any fairy connection but that guy who sits in his library and reads and tries to bind everything in a perfect organization...(Order of hermes..) well that's ok?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T10:55:01-08:00","id":1177364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177357#post1177357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quint/Glamour/Gnosis are game mechanics to cover &amp;quot;Magic shit pool&amp;quot; if you'd prefer it gets renamed &amp;quot;magic shit pool&amp;quot; when someone is a kinain go right ahead.<br /> <br /> I see no reason for two pools. I see no reason to not allow them to use their generic magic pool multiple ways because they are Kinain. I see no reason to give mages or werewolves arts and realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you need to give arts and realms, but I also see no reason to ban it for the kinain fera. <br /> <br /> Having the pool be the same makes no sense though. It would imply that freeholds and cairns are the same thing, for instance, which they pretty clearly not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T12:09:43-08:00","id":1177380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177358#post1177358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's whole damned faction of Etherites called &quot;Adventurers&quot; so yeah someone who's hunted dinosaurs in the Hollow Earth is considered too banal to have any fairy connection but that guy who sits in his library and reads and tries to bind everything in a perfect organization...(Order of hermes..) well that's ok?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not forget the Mad Scientists.<br /> <br /> And Zenten, while a freehold and cairn are two vastly different things the the fera and the fae, to most mages, they're just different flavors of nodes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23716-scottish","name":"Scottish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T12:22:16-08:00","id":1177385,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with Glamour being Quintessence plus extra stuff Mages describe as &quot;resonance&quot;. But you need transmutation to turn most quintessence into Glamour, or Banality.<br /> <br /> And I mean, under the purple paradigm everything is really just Quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","user":"zenten","date":". 01-19-2018, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T13:53:30-08:00","id":1177404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177385#post1177385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with Glamour being Quintessence plus extra stuff Mages describe as &quot;resonance&quot;. But you need transmutation to turn most quintessence into Glamour, or Banality.<br /> <br /> And I mean, under the purple paradigm everything is really just Quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we're back to why people being willing to talk to you is important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23716-scottish","name":"Scottish","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23716_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T15:00:54-08:00","id":1177426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scottish</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177404#post1177404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And we're back to why people being willing to talk to you is important.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand. Kinain are rarely if ever given Glamour by the Kithain. A prodigal with something to trade would be in a better position to aquire Dross or a Freehold, kinain or not.<br /> <br /> Now, a permanently enchanted Kinain prodigal yes, that would be useful.<br /> <br /> Also, I really don't think fairy affinity is the same at all as being kinain. There's nothing in it about seeing Chimerical reality or immunity to the mists, and the kinain aren't automatically allies of the Kithain like kinfolk are to the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T15:32:22-08:00","id":1177440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177426#post1177426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, I really don't think fairy affinity is the same at all as being kinain. There's nothing in it about seeing Chimerical reality or immunity to the mists, and the kinain aren't automatically allies of the Kithain like kinfolk are to the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again we, or atleast I, are not talking about Faerie Affinity, M20 Book of Secrets p.69, but of Fae Blood, M20 Book of Secrets p.74. The first one is not Kinain but rather someone whom for reasons unknown the Fae find to be more appealing and from whom it is easier to draw Glamour from and to enchant while the latter specifically is about being permanently enchanted due to having faerie blood and it also specifically states that in Changeling terms you are a Kinain.<br /> <br /> Also kinfolk are not automatically allied with their Garou kin. No more than Kinain are allied with Changelings. In fact some of the most dangerous Garou hunters are kinfolk, the most infamous ofcourse being the, dare I invoke his accursed name, one and only Samuel Haight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T22:35:53-08:00","id":1177528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177364#post1177364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you need to give arts and realms, but I also see no reason to ban it for the kinain fera.<br /> <br /> Having the pool be the same makes no sense though. It would imply that freeholds and cairns are the same thing, for instance, which they pretty clearly not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all Freeholds and Caerns match up, this is true. But there are Freeholds.. well GLENS that are Double dipped as both. Same with there are Nodes that have Changelings and Mages drawing from the same well. Unless you are a changeling and then &quot;Yes werewolves sacred sites are potential freeholds&quot;<br /> <br /> And it has nothing to do with Caerns and Freeholds being the same thing. It has to do with As a Werewolf with some faery Blood your Gnosis pool isn't quite like normal werewolves. IF EVERY werewolf could readily interact as I'm saying Kinain should then your argument would be the case. But its not. But since they aren't fairies, they are primarily werewolves.<br /> <br /> I could also make the argument that Fairy blood should do nothing since you can't be a Kithain and Kinain at the same time as Changeling treats Protigals as lost and twisted Kiths rather than separate supernatural beings and this is Changeling..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T06:00:35-07:00","id":1232354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1177385#post1177385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with Glamour being Quintessence plus extra stuff Mages describe as &quot;resonance&quot;. But you need transmutation to turn most quintessence into Glamour, or Banality.<br /> <br /> And I mean, under the purple paradigm everything is really just Quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why you Never go purple paradigm.<br /> <br /> From purple paradigm, the only thing that separates Anyone from using changeling, Garou, or Vampire powers is what flavor of Quintessence is in their system and a prime sphere user plays with resonance as their day job.<br /> <br /> This is mage we're talking about, where you can use a prime rote to prepare pre-roled spells like a D&amp;D wizard, move crap on the fly with your mind like you're psychic, or create a bunch of technological implants/devices that give you super-cyborg powers. It's notorious for spinning the balance of other games for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T06:27:31-07:00","id":1232357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1232354#post1232354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is why you Never go purple paradigm.<br /> <br /> From purple paradigm, the only thing that separates Anyone from using changeling, Garou, or Vampire powers is what flavor of Quintessence is in their system and a prime sphere user plays with resonance as their day job.<br /> <br /> This is mage we're talking about, where you can use a prime rote to prepare pre-roled spells like a D&amp;D wizard, move crap on the fly with your mind like you're psychic, or create a bunch of technological implants/devices that give you super-cyborg powers. It's notorious for spinning the balance of other games for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything in Mage is the Purple Paradigm plus restrictions on what you can do. It's how the system works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-04T07:59:33-07:00","id":1232376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1173250-c20-kinain-prodigals?p=1232357#post1232357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything in Mage is the Purple Paradigm plus restrictions on what you can do. It's how the system works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily that cut-and-dry unfortunately. Depending on the edition and author of the book you're reading, mage books can very wildly in cosmological view from things like Consensus=reality vs reality=underlying reality+consensus to how many spheres there are to whether or not things other then humans have avatars. It's messy and confusing even in the same edition.<br /> <br /> Not even getting into details of things like awakening and avatars that have never been explained.<br /> <br /> Though I originally said that as purple paradigm not being fun to play. Besides, in a consensual reality whatever your paradigm is, it's true in relation to You at least if not so for the wider world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}